feat(pick): glue-aware insertion — 's attaches, punctuation gets a space

Candidates now carry whether their seed token had a leading space
(glue). New pure planPick(before, candidate) plans the pick edit:
consume trailing spaces/tabs before the cursor, then insert either the
glued candidate directly after the previous word ("Paris " + 's ->
"Paris's ") or a normal word with exactly one separating space — added
even when the user typed none (punctuation trigger "It rains." ->
"It rains. The "), never at line/document start. Deepening joins
prompt + (glue ? '' : ' ') + candidate to match. candidateAt returns
the full Candidate; main.ts pick dispatches the planned change.

